    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **45 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'`, dropping the per-city sequence numbers entirely.\n\n### Changes (all in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)\n\n1. **`assignCustomerCode` rewritten** \u2014 it now takes the region, normalized telephone, and last name, and returns `region + \"-\" + HASH8`, where `HASH8` is the first 8 upper-case hex characters of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`. The old `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` format and the owner-counting sequence logic (and the now-unused `prefix3` helper) are gone, replaced by a `sha256UpperHex` helper.\n\n2. **Call site in `addOwner`** \u2014 computes `region = Localities.region(postcode, city)` (the postcode-preferred derivation shared with the locality) and passes it, plus the already-normalized E.164 telephone and last name, into `assignCustomerCode`.\n\n3. **Stale javadoc** on `rejectCityAtCapacity` updated (it referenced the old counting behaviour of `assignCustomerCode`).\n\n### Why the derived values just follow along\n- **Membership number** (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) and **check digit** (Luhn over the code's digits) are computed from `customerCode` in `OwnerMapper`, so they now reflect the region-and-hash code automatically.\n- **Audit record** logs `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so it now carries `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (visible in the run: `customerCode=NSW-F4F6FF62`).\n- **Locality** already resolves via `Localities.region(postcode, city)` \u2014 the exact same region derivation the identity's `REGION` now uses, so identity and locality are consistent (Sydney/2000 \u2192 NSW; unknown city + 3000 \u2192 VIC).\n\nBoth the eight directly-affected checkpoints and the full 45-test suite pass.",
